= Reich Intervention in Saxony

On 29 October, President Ebert uses his emergency powers against Saxony. Troops march into Dresden and a Reich commissioner removes Zeigner's government. Thuringia's KPD ministers leave office soon afterwards. The Bavarian government, openly defying Berlin from the right, faces no such action.

The SPD left the Stresemann cabinet in protest. Many SPD workers are angry at their own leaders, which is a small opening for the united front.
